# Installed dependencies. package-lock.json IS committed, so `npm ci` reproduces.
#
# `node_modules` WITHOUT A TRAILING SLASH, anywhere (2026-09-16). `node_modules/`
# matches only a directory, so a worktree whose node_modules was a SYMLINK to
# another checkout's had it committed by a `git add -A` (9d7ebd0). A checkout
# that then merged that commit had its real, ignored node_modules directory
# REPLACED by the link — git treats ignored files as disposable — and the link
# pointed at itself. This pattern matches a file, a link and a directory alike.
node_modules

# Generated at runtime, never committed: the signing keys are regenerated on every
# start by design (see README.md — a per-run kid is what stops a stale instance and
# a fresh one both claiming the same kid over different keys).
*.pem
*.log

# THE PERSISTENT STORE, since 2026-08-27. `persistence.mode=ldif` writes one
# RFC 2849 LDIF file per trust realm here, plus realms.json and appconfig.json.
# Never committed, and the reason is the same one that keeps the console from
# rewriting env/*.js: a directory or a setting somebody changed while trying
# something out would otherwise arrive in the repository and become everybody's
# default. `persistence.dataDir` moves it; in a container it is a volume.
data/

# THE TEST REPORT and the coverage report, both generated and both timestamped.
# `./docker-run-tests.sh` writes tests/report/<mode>/<run>/ and points
# tests/report/<mode>/latest at it (`./local-run-tests.sh` wrote there too until
# it was removed on 2026-09-16); `./run-coverage.sh` writes its own run under
# tests/report/ and writes coverage/, including coverage/raw/ — V8's own JSON,
# which is tens of megabytes per run. Neither is committed for the reason
# the data directory above is not: a report is a claim about ONE run on ONE
# machine, and a stale one in the repository would be read as a claim about the
# code it sits beside.
tests/report/
coverage/

# THE BUILD STAMP. `common/version.js --stamp .` writes version.json at the
# package root during the image build, and it is what every surface here reports
# as the version — see CLAUDE.md, *Versioning*. It is never committed for the
# reason the report above is not: it is a claim about ONE build on ONE machine,
# and a stale one in the repository would make every checkout claim to be an
# artifact that was built somewhere else. With no stamp the version is computed
# at startup and says so, which is the correct answer for a checkout.
#
# ANCHORED, so it names the one file at the package root and not any file of
# that name anywhere in the tree. There is only one stamp: `xacml-pep/`
# deliberately does not get one, for a reason common/version.js gives.
/version.json

# THE EMBEDDED PROTOCOL DEBUGGER'S BUILT TREE (2026-09-13). The debugger
# project's `embedded/build.sh --out debugger/embedded` writes it for a checkout
# run, and the image copies the same tree out of that project's embedded image
# instead. It is the other repository's build output — its own node_modules
# included — and never this one's source.
debugger/embedded/

# The one native module (#40): compiled inside an image build only, by
# build-native.sh, and never committed or sent from a host.
spiffe/native/*.node
